  "description": "T1 Oak (Quercus spp.) Selective crown management works including the removal of dead, damaged and defective branches throughout the canopy and selective pruning of crossing and rubbing branches where appropriate. Carry out a light crown thin to improve light penetration through the canopy whilst maintaining the tree's natural form, amenity value and physiological health. No more than 15% thinning from branch ends. T2 Southern Magnolia (Magnolia grandiflora): Removal of deadwood throughout the crown and light formative pruning to improve crown structure and encourage healthy future growth whilst retaining the tree's natural shape and ornamental characteristics. T3 Lime (Tilia spp.) (Neighbouring Tree): Reduce branches overhanging the applicant's garden back to suitable growth points (2m from branch ends) in order to contain growth within the available space, improve light penetration to the rear garden and maintain an appropriate relationship with neighbouring land use.",
